@startuml
' PlantUML preview test fixture — the whole file is one diagram.
'
' Expected with PlantUML drawing ON:  renders as an image served from a data: URI.
'                                     Confirm in DevTools that the <img> src starts
'                                     with "data:" and is NOT https://www.plantuml.com —
'                                     a host in img-src would hand every previewed
'                                     file a beacon channel.
' Expected with drawing OFF:          the source shows with a note saying why, and
'                                     NOTHING leaves the machine. That is the whole
'                                     point of the setting: "off" means the source
'                                     must not travel, and showing it locally honours
'                                     that while still being useful.
'
' This file is deliberately over 4 KB. The old ~h hex URL form doubled the source and
' the server answered HTTP 400 somewhere past an 8 KB URL, so every .puml over roughly
' 3.5 KB — most real diagrams — failed to render. If this one draws, the deflate +
' custom-base64 path via CompressionStream('deflate-raw') is working. If it 400s, the
' code fell back to hex.
'
' There is a fence on the next line on purpose: ``` — a standalone .puml must not be
' wrapped in a synthetic fenced block and run through the markdown renderer.

title Previewing an attachment, end to end

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Reader" as User
participant "Google Chat\n(page DOM)" as Chat
participant "content.js\n(isolated world)" as Content
participant "background.js\n(service worker)" as Worker
participant "Chat attachment API" as Api
participant "sandbox.html\n(opaque origin)" as Sandbox
participant "attachment frame\n(srcdoc)" as Frame
participant "PlantUML server" as Puml

== Detection ==

Chat -> Content : message list mutates\n(virtualized: mounted and unmounted while scrolling)
activate Content
Content -> Content : debounced MutationObserver scan
note right of Content
  Never key off CSS class names —
  they are build-generated and change
  between releases. Match the
  get_attachment_url endpoint instead,
  host- and path-agnostically:
  chat.google.com/api/...
  chat.google.com/u/0/api/...  (multi-account)
  mail.google.com/chat/api/...  (Gmail)
end note
Content -> Content : read content_type + alt / aria-label / download
note right of Content
  The detailed-thread card has no <img>
  at all. The file name lives only on an
  ancestor div[role="button"] title or
  aria-label, which is why the walk up
  ANCESTOR_LABEL_DEPTH levels exists.
  Drop it and that whole view goes
  undetectable — silently.
end note
Content -> Content : extension decides the kind\n(content_type is only a fallback)
note right of Content
  Chat reports .md as text/plain and often
  reports .html as application/octet-stream.
  For .mmd and .puml there is no fallback at
  all — every diagram extension is served as
  text/plain.
end note
Content -> Chat : inject Preview button\ninto a CLOSED shadow root
note right of Content
  :host { all: initial } — Chat's stylesheet
  is aggressive enough to break unshielded UI
  on Google's next release.
  Deduplicated per scan on attachment_token,
  the only stable identity.
end note
deactivate Content

== Fetching the bytes ==

User -> Chat : clicks Preview
Chat -> Content : click
activate Content
Content -> Worker : FETCH_ATTACHMENT { url }
activate Worker

group Service worker first
  Worker -> Api : GET url_type=DOWNLOAD_URL
  Api --> Worker : 302 to a Google file-serving host
  Worker -> Api : follow redirect
  note right of Worker
    Only this context can follow it.
    A page-context fetch starts same-origin,
    becomes cross-origin at the redirect, and
    dies with a bare TypeError: Failed to fetch
    because those hosts send no
    Access-Control-Allow-Origin.
    Every possible redirect target must be in
    host_permissions, not just the endpoint host.
  end note
  Api --> Worker : bytes
end

alt worker path fails
  Worker --> Content : error (url_type + host/path, no query string)
  Content -> Api : same request from the page
  note right of Content
    The only context that sends Origin and
    Referer. A service worker fetch cannot set
    Referer at all — forbidden header — so if
    the API starts requiring it, this is the
    path that still works.
  end note
  Api --> Content : bytes or error
  note over Content
    When BOTH fail, report BOTH errors.
    Returning only the page-context error hides
    the worker's and makes a CORS failure look
    like an API rejection — that cost a full
    debugging round once already.
  end note
end

deactivate Worker

== Rendering ==

Content -> Sandbox : postMessage { kind, source, settings }
note right of Content
  A string. Never inserted into the Chat DOM.
  Settings travel in the message because the
  sandbox has no chrome.* APIs.
end note
deactivate Content

activate Sandbox
Sandbox -> Sandbox : re-check the kind\n(do not trust the message)
Sandbox -> Sandbox : buildDocument(...)\nrenderMermaid and fetchDiagram injected

group PlantUML only — the source leaves the machine
  Sandbox -> Content : DIAGRAM_REQUEST { id, source }
  activate Content
  Content -> Worker : fetch diagram
  activate Worker
  Worker -> Puml : GET /png/<deflate + custom base64>
  Puml --> Worker : image bytes
  Worker --> Content : data: URI
  deactivate Worker
  Content --> Sandbox : DIAGRAM_RESULT { id, dataUri }
  deactivate Content
  note over Sandbox
    Ids matter: several diagrams in one
    document resolve concurrently and out
    of order. The relay exists because the
    sandbox has no chrome.* APIs.
  end note
end

Sandbox -> Frame : rebuild the frame from scratch,\nset srcdoc
note right of Sandbox
  The sandbox attribute is read at load time
  only, so mutating a live frame would keep
  the old permissions.
  sandbox="" unless the kind is html AND the
  user opted in.
end note
deactivate Sandbox

activate Frame
Frame -> User : the preview
Frame -->x Puml : blocked (img-src is data: blob:)
Frame -->x Chat : blocked (no allow-same-origin)
deactivate Frame

legend right
  If this legend and every note above are
  legible, a source well past the old 8 KB
  URL ceiling round-tripped successfully.
end legend

@enduml
